# Custom Suricata rules developed for this project.
# Deployed via pfSense: Services -> Suricata -> OPT1 -> Rules -> Custom
# See REMEDIATION.md for full rationale, deployment steps, and before/after evidence.

# Rule 1 — MQTT unauthorized connection attempt.
# Matches the MQTT CONNECT control packet type byte (0x10) arriving at the
# broker's port. Confirmed effective — see FINDINGS.md test #9.
alert tcp any any -> 192.168.30.20 1883 (msg:"CUSTOM Unauthorized MQTT Connection Attempt"; flow:to_server,established; content:"|10|"; offset:0; depth:1; sid:9000001; rev:1;)

# Rule 2 — Telnet rapid brute-force pattern (login timeout).
# Content match derived directly from a tcpdump capture of BusyBox telnetd's
# actual behavior under an automated brute-force attempt (it does not send a
# standard login prompt in this scenario; it sends this literal message
# before tearing down the connection). Deployed and confirmed enabled, but
# did NOT fire even against confirmed-live logging. Left in place as a
# documented, unresolved false negative — see FINDINGS.md test #10 and
# REMEDIATION.md section 3 for the full investigation.
alert tcp any any -> 192.168.30.20 2323 (msg:"CUSTOM Telnet Rapid Brute-Force Pattern (Login Timeout)"; flow:to_client,established; content:"Login timed out"; sid:9000002; rev:2;)
